---

<section class="section" id="services">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section-head">
			<span class="eyebrow">01 — What we build</span>
			<h2 class="section-title">Five layers. One standard of excellence.</h2>
			<p class="section-sub">
				From the lamp that turns on at dusk to the platform that runs your company — each engagement is engineered,
				built, integrated and proven.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="services-grid">
			<article class="service-card">
				<div class="service-top">
					<span class="service-num">/ 01</span>
				</div>
				<h3 class="service-title">Home Automation</h3>
				<p class="service-tag">From voice to everything.</p>
				<p class="service-desc">
					Whole-home automation designed around how you actually live — scenes, routines, voice and app control,
					all on a hub architecture that scales.
				</p>
				<ul class="service-list">
					<li>Needs assessment &amp; hub architecture</li>
					<li>Device selection &amp; whole-home scenes</li>
					<li>Voice &amp; app integration</li>
					<li>Install, test, handoff</li>
				</ul>
			</article>

			<article class="service-card">
				<div class="service-top">
					<span class="service-num">/ 02</span>
				</div>
				<h3 class="service-title">Website Building</h3>
				<p class="service-tag">Fast. Sharp. Shipped.</p>
				<p class="service-desc">
					Marketing sites and web apps on modern stacks like Astro — built to load instantly and convert without
					bloated tooling.
				</p>
				<ul class="service-list">
					<li>Architecture &amp; UX before design</li>
					<li>Design + build</li>
					<li>Content, deploy &amp; analytics handoff</li>
				</ul>
			</article>

			<article class="service-card">
				<div class="service-top">
					<span class="service-num">/ 03</span>
				</div>
				<h3 class="service-title">Networking</h3>
				<p class="service-tag">Wired. Wireless. Secure.</p>
				<p class="service-desc">
					Coverage, performance and segmentation — wired drops, mesh wireless, VLANs and firewall rules that keep
					the network clean under load.
				</p>
				<ul class="service-list">
					<li>Site survey &amp; AP / PoE design</li>
					<li>Wired + mesh wireless</li>
					<li>VLANs, firewall, VPN segmentation</li>
					<li>Docs &amp; handover</li>
				</ul>
			</article>

			<article class="service-card">
				<div class="service-top">
					<span class="service-num">/ 04</span>
				</div>
				<h3 class="service-title">Security &amp; Pentest</h3>
				<p class="service-tag">Scan. Report. Fix.</p>
				<p class="service-desc">
					Scans and assessments across the stack you actually run — network, web, cloud and the devices in your
					home or office — with reports written in plain language.
				</p>
				<ul class="service-list">
					<li>Network, web &amp; cloud posture scans</li>
					<li>IoT / device audits</li>
					<li>Plain-English report + remediation</li>
					<li>Retest after fixes</li>
				</ul>
			</article>

			<article class="service-card">
				<div class="service-top">
					<span class="service-num">/ 05</span>
				</div>
				<h3 class="service-title">AI Help</h3>
				<p class="service-tag">Assistants that actually help.</p>
				<p class="service-desc">
					AI assistants and workflows that take real work off your plate — grounded in your own docs, wired into
					the systems you already have.
				</p>
				<ul class="service-list">
					<li>AI workflows for ops &amp; support</li>
					<li>Assistants grounded in your docs</li>
					<li>Home ops automation where useful</li>
				</ul>
			</article>

			<article class="service-card">
				<div class="service-top">
					<span class="service-num">/ 06</span>
				</div>
				<h3 class="service-title">Home + Business Builds</h3>
				<p class="service-tag">One standard, both worlds.</p>
				<p class="service-desc">
					The same engineering standard applied to a house and to an office — so the system you build at home is the
					system you can run at work, and vice versa.
				</p>
				<ul class="service-list">
					<li>Audits for home + business stacks</li>
					<li>Unified architecture plans</li>
					<li>Cross-environment automation</li>
				</ul>
			</article>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
